      <div type="clause" n="75">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 75</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="75" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="122" ed="#liebermann"/>CXVIIII. Gif mon ceap befehþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.10-2"/> forstolenne, ⁊ sio hond tiemð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.11-2"/> þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi>, sio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.12"/> hine mon ætbefehþ, to oþrum men<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.13"/>, gif se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.14"/> mon hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.15"/> þon<hi rend="italic">ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.14"/></hi> onfon ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.16"/> wille ⁊ sægþ, þæt he him næfre þæt ne sealde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.17"/>, ac sealde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.17"/> oþer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.18"/>, þonne mot se gecyðan, se ðe hit tiemþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.11-2"/> to þære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.19"/> honda, þæt he him nan oðer ne sealde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.17"/> buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.20"/> þæt ilce.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="75" corresp="#wit-ot-frags"><pb n="122" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif ....p be ....llenne, ⁊ ::: hond tymþ, ..:io hine mon ætbef::ð, to oþr ..., ... mon hine .... wille ⁊ sægþ, .... þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ne sealde, :c sealde oþer, :onne mot ...., se þe hit tiemþ to þære hond:, ..sealde buton þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ylce.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="75" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="122" ed="#liebermann"/>CXIX. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.2-2"/> ceap befehð forstolenne, ⁊ seo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.4-2"/> hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.2-2"/> tymð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.5-2"/> þonne, seo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.6-2"/> hine mon ætbefehð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.7-2"/>, to oþrum men, gif se mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.2-2"/> hine þonne onfon nylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.5-2"/> (þæs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.8-2"/> ceapes) ⁊ sægð, þæt he him næfre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.9-2"/> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ne sealde, ac sealde oðer, þonne mot se gecyðan se ðe hit tymð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.5-2"/> to þære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.9-2"/> honda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.2-2"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he him nan oþer ne sealde buton ðæt ilce.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="75" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="123" ed="#liebermann"/>Be forstolene ceape. Gyf mon ceap befehþ forstolene, ⁊ seo hand tymð ðonne, seo hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.star2"/> mon ætbefehð ðe to oðrum men, gyf se mon hine onfon nylle ⁊ sægð, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he him næfre þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ne sealde, ac sealde oðer, ðonne [mot<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.1"/>] se ge[cyþan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.2"/>, se] ðe hit tymð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.3"/> to ðara handa, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he him nan oðer ne sealde buton þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ilce.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="75" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="123" ed="#liebermann"/>Si captale<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.4"/> (quodlibet) intercietur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.5"/> furtiuum, et ille super quem intercietur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.6"/> aduocet inde, si aduocatus nolit hoc recipere et dicat, quod nunquam hoc ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.7"/> uendidit, sed aliud, tunc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.8"/> licebit aduocanti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.9"/> (appellantem) ipsam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.10"/> manum in uerum mittere, quod nullum aliud uendidit ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.10"/> quam id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_75.lnote.oe.11"/> ipsum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="60" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be forstolene ceape.] Gif mon ceap befehþ forstolenne, ⁊ sio hond tiemð þonne, sio hine mon ætbefehþ, to<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Ine_75.attnote.fn.9"/> oþrum men, gif se mon hine þonne<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_75.attnote.fn.2"/> onfon ne wille<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Ine_75.attnote.fn.10"/><ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Ine_75.attnote.fn.11"/> ⁊ sægþ, þæt he him næfre þæt ne sealde, ac sealde oþer, þonne mot se gecyðan, se ðe hit tiemþ to þære<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Ine_75.attnote.fn.12"/> honda, þæt he him nan oðer ne sealde buton þæt ilce.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="77" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="436" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{CXVIIII} Gif mon ceap befehþ forstolenne, ⁊ sio hond tiemð þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> sio hine mon ætbefehþ to oþrum men: gif se mon hine þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> onfon ne wille ⁊ sægþ þæt he him næfre þæt ne sealde ac sealde oþer, þonne mot se gecyðan se ðe hit tiemþ to þære honda, þæt he him nan oðer ne sealde buton þæt ilce.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="123" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn gestohlenes Gut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_75.lnote.de.1"/> im Anefang<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_75.lnote.de.2"/> gefasst wird, und die Person, bei der<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_75.lnote.de.3"/> es gefasst wird, zieht nun die Gewähr auf einen andern Mann: wenn dieser Mann jenes [Zugeschobene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_75.lnote.de.4"/>] dann nicht annehmen will und sagt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_75.lnote.de.5"/>, dass er ihm dieses nie verkauft habe, vielmehr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_75.lnote.de.6"/> [etwas] anderes verkauft habe, dann darf, wer es zu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_75.lnote.de.7"/> dieser Person [in Gewähr] zieht, [durch Eid] beweisen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_75.lnote.de.8"/>, dass er [der herangezogene Gewährsmann] ihm kein anderes als dieses selbe verkauft hat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If stolen goods are seized by attachment, and the person from whom they are seized now vouches to warranty upon another man: if that man will not accept that [which is vouched to him] and says that he never sold him this, but sold him something else, then whoever vouches it to that person [as warrantor] may prove [by oath] that he [the warrantor called upon] sold him nothing other than this very thing.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="61" ed="#attenborough"/>If a stolen chattel<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_75.attnote.n.1"/> is attached, and the person in whose possession it is attached vouches it to another man, and if the man will not admit it, and says that he never sold him that, but that he sold him some other thing, he who vouched the man to warranty may declare that he [the witness] sold him none other but that same thing.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="408" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone attaches stolen property, and the person with whom it is attached vouches another man to warranty, if that man will not admit it and says he never sold it to him, but sold him something else, then he who is vouching that person to warranty may declare that he sold him nothing other than that same thing.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="437" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If stolen goods are seized, and then the man [<hi rend="italic">hand</hi>] in whose possession the goods were seized vouches a second man to warranty: if the second man will not accept it and says that he never sold him that [property in question] but sold him something else, then he who vouches [him] to warranty must declare, that he sold him none other than that same [property].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="436"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_35">Ine 35</ref> <quote>Compare to §35.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="437"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Hl_16">Hl 16</ref> <quote>Liebermann believes this clause may contain traces of oath formulae. Compare to Hloþhere and Eadric §11 [L16].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>gloss to</label> <ref target="clause:Af_22">Af 22</ref> <quote>Up to forty ... items ... look like glosses to Ine (n. 78: add Af 22 compared to Ine 8 (or 13, 35:1, 75))</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">123</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">umzustellen</hi> ðe hine m. æ., to</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to be transposed: ðe hine m. æ., to</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">123</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. übergeschrieben</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">123</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hinter</hi> sege <hi rend="italic">Rasur etwa zweier Buchstaben; im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. am Rande:</hi> cyþan se</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure of about two letters after sege; in the margin in the 16th cent.: cyþan se</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">123</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">spät geänd. aus</hi> cymð</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered late from cymð</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">123</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> furt. ca. in. <hi rend="italic">übrige ohne</hi> qu.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; furt. ca. in. the others, without qu.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">123</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ciatur <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ciatur R</seg></note>
