        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oðre <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oðre So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðara handa <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðara handa Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">butan þ. ylce <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">butan þ. ylce So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Vieh’ zwar zunächst, aber zu eng; gemeint ist ‘Fahrhabe’, auch Sklav</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Cattle’ in the first instance, it is true, but too narrow; what is meant is ‘movable property’, including a slave</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Anefang 21. Nach späteren Quellen leistet Beklagter vor dem Gewährzug Sicherheit für dessen Rechtmässigkeit; <hi rend="italic">ebd.</hi> 10. — Q braucht Fränkische Termini technici</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Anefang 21. According to later sources the defendant, before vouching to warranty, gives security for its lawfulness; <hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi> 10. — Q uses Frankish technical terms</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Anakoluth ist statt Obliquus des Relativs dieser Nominativ; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Wb</hi> 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This nominative, instead of an oblique case of the relative, is an anacoluthon; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘jenes [strittige] Gut’ schiebt Hcor., das Pron. <hi rend="italic">hine</hi> erläuternd, ein; sowohl Acc. wie Gen. kann <hi rend="italic">onfón</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi> 5) regieren</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘that [disputed] property’ is inserted by Hcor., explaining the pron. <hi rend="italic">hine</hi>; <hi rend="italic">onfón</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi> 5) can govern either the acc. or the gen.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wohl Wortlaut der Eidesformel; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4 II</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Probably the wording of the oath formula; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4 II</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wohl Wortlaut der Eidesformel; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4 II</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Probably the wording of the oath formula; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4 II</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Kläger gelangt also zwar hier zum Eide, aber nur falls Bezogener einen Handel mit Beklagtem überhaupt zugibt. — In Q ist <hi rend="italic">manum</hi> (Bezogenen) Objekt zu <hi rend="italic">advocanti</hi> (<hi rend="italic">appellantem</hi>) (Gewähr ziehenden). — B hatte vor Korrektur kürzer: ‘dann sage wer es’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The plaintiff thus does, it is true, come to the oath here, but only if the man vouched admits any dealing with the defendant at all. — In Q <hi rend="italic">manum</hi> (the man vouched) is the object of <hi rend="italic">advocanti</hi> (<hi rend="italic">appellantem</hi>) (the one vouching to warranty). — B before correction had more briefly: ‘then let someone say it’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_75.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wohl Wortlaut der Eidesformel; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4 II</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Probably the wording of the oath formula; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4 II</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_75.attnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>þonne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">om. B.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 2 is printed 2 times on the page (74.1, 75), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_75.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>to</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðe to</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_75.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>wille</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">nylle</hi>. H &amp; B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_75.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>wille</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">nylle</hi> (<hi rend="italic">þæs ceapes</hi>). H*.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_75.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>þære</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðara</hi>. B &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_75.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">193</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Schmid translates ‘Vieh (Gut).’ The law relates primarily, no doubt, but not exclusively to cattle.</seg></note>
